.TH UMS-RENDERER 1 "November 2026" "kcm-ums 0.2.0"
.SH NAME
ums-renderer \- select and control a Universal Media Server renderer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ums-renderer
.RB [ --target " tv|headset" ]
.RB [ --server " URL" ]
.RB [ -- ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens an explicit selector for devices already known to Universal Media Server.
A selected file must already belong to the UMS shared library.
The program does not enable sharing or start a separate media server.
The selected renderer is exposed through MPRIS2 for Plasma media controls.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --target " group"
Filter the selector to televisions and other non-headset renderers
.RB ( tv )
or Flat Headset and StereoDroid renderers
.RB ( headset ).
.TP
.BI --server " URL"
Use the specified UMS web interface.
By default, use the local interface and the web_gui_port in UMS.conf.
Use HTTPS when sending credentials to a remote server.
.TP
.B --help
Show command-line help.
.SH FILES
UMS.conf and SHARED.conf in the UMS profile directory are read without
changing their contents.
UMS_PROFILE overrides the normal XDG configuration location.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Virtual, flattened, renamed or ambiguous library entries may be refused
rather than matched by guessing.
Control uses UPnP transport instance 0.
.SH AUTHORS
Daniel Campos Ramos, for Sparky Stereo OS.
Universal Media Server, jUPnP, KDE Frameworks and MPRIS provide the underlying interfaces.
